The Broker is the leader of the [[Org/Althane/The Network|Network]], and the name its clients know best. A hood is drawn up over their face; beneath it they are dark metal with wooden fittings, and a symbol no one has read is stamped into their forehead.

They keep to themselves, working through the handlers of their cells. A library serves as their own, book stacks on either side of a long table; a two-headed dragon, [[People/Althane/Terexanthes|Terexanthes]], stands with them there, and so does a man in a suit whose head is a burst of green flame. When scrying spells fell twice on one of the Broker's people, the Broker pulled that operative back. Their rooms in [[Geography/Althane/Illyara/index|Illyara]] belong to [[People/Althane/Oxus|Oxus]].

The Broker's true name is Tech, spelled on the door of their hall as T3C, and they are of [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]], whose people come from the antimatter world of [[Geography/Ushas|Ushas]] and wear charms to keep from destroying ordinary matter at a touch. They belong to no local [[Phenomena/Weave|weave]], so a mage feels nothing of them. They keep a citadel in open space, [[Geography/Elysium|Elysium]], and carry a dead [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessian]], one of the good ones, tethered to them.

They hired [[Org/Althane/The Weft|the Weft]] to recover the [[Phenomena/Althane/The Gun|gun]] out of the [[Org/Althane/The First House|First House]], an artifact that once put a hole through their own body. They used the leech inside the gun to close that wound and handed the gun back to the Weft, who carry it now. They hunt an [[Phenomena/Echo Fragment|Echo Fragment]] against the will of [[Divinity/The Narrative/index|the Narrative]].

They travel by a flash of blue light, and they cut chrome into their own people. The Broker keeps a surgery theater in [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)/Terminus|Terminus]], where they work alone, strapping a client down and guiding the tools with a gloved hand, opening the skull, fitting the implant, and knitting the bone back with a little necromancy. The same hand did the work on their own head, and they trust no one else with it. They also know a magic that rewrites a witness's memory, and they keep a short list of loose ends they mean to close.
